\pard\sa200\sl276\slmult1\b\f0\fs32\lang9 Name: Muhammad Reshail\par
Class: BSAI(4A)-053\par
\par
 Introduction:\b0\par
 \fs22 This project presents an AI chatbot designed for a restaurant named Foodie's Paradise. The chatbot \par
simulates natural conversation with users and provides quick responses to queries regarding the menu, \par
drinks, desserts, and table bookings using a semantic similarity approach.\par
 Objective\par
 \f1\bullet  Build an interactive AI chatbot that understands user queries.\par
 \bullet  Provide accurate and fun responses about food items and services.\par
 \bullet  Improve customer experience using NLP and transformer models.\par
 Working\par
\b  Step 1: Define Question-Answer Pool\b0\par
 Predefined questions and fun answers were created for topics like:\par
 \bullet  Menu overview\par
 \bullet  Burgers, pizzas, pasta, biryani\par
 \bullet  BBQ, desserts, drinks\par
 \bullet  Booking a table\par
\b  Step 2: Load Semantic Model\b0\par
 The chatbot uses the sentence-transformers library with the all-MiniLM-L6-v2 model to \par
convert user inputs and predefined questions into embeddings.\par
\b  Step 3: Calculate Similarity\b0\par
 The chatbot calculates the cosine similarity between user input and each question. If the best match \par
exceeds a defined threshold (e.g., 0.4), the corresponding answer is returned.\par
\b  Step 4: User Interaction Loop\b0\par
 The chatbot continuously takes input until the user types 'bye', 'exit', or 'quit'\par
\par

